WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.247
Sometimes diplomacy
is downright hard.

00:00:02.247 --> 00:00:04.080
You're dealing with
people that you'd really

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:05.500
rather not be dealing with.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.065
I haven't seen
you lose it ever.

00:00:11.432 --> 00:00:13.140
My relationship with
Madeleine Albright

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.460
goes well back before either
of us was Secretary of State.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.102
I was a failed piano major
at the University of Denver.

00:00:21.102 --> 00:00:23.310
I was about to end up teaching
13-year-olds to murder

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.710
Beethoven for a living and
I needed something else,

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.950
and I wandered into a course
in international politics

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:30.990
taught by a man
named Josef Korbel.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:32.520
He was Madeline's father.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.452
He opened up the world to
me of things diplomatic.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:37.410
It's a pretty amazing story

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.380
that this refugee
diplomat basically trained

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:42.990
two women Secretaries of State.

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:46.050
When I found out she was a
Republican, I said Condi,

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:46.860
"how could you be?

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.300
We have the same father."

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.650
When you're a
diplomat, you need

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.530
to build consensus often with
people with whom you disagree.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.750
It is personal,
in a lot of ways,

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:03.570
because you do have to get to
know the people, put yourself

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:05.760
into the shoes of the
person and the country

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:09.180
that you're dealing with so that
you can come to some agreement.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.952
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:17.130
Finding common ground, working
with people who are different--

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.680
those are skills that you
can use in everyday life,

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.820
in whatever you do.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:23.570
[MUSIC PLAYING]

